course: dictionary
lesson: 13844
title: Jimmy, a name, a tool, and a word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Look at the words around it to find which one the writer means. «The burglar carried a jimmy, a short metal bar with a flat end.» Here a jimmy is a tool, because a burglar is someone who breaks into buildings.
explain: The word can also be a verb, an action word. «The burglar jimmied the back window open in the night.» To jimmy means to force something open with a bar or tool. The clues are burglar and window, so the meaning fits.
explain: Sometimes jimmy is a name. «Jimmy is a short, friendly form of James.» In Scotland, «Hey, Jimmy!» can be a friendly or cheeky way to call a man you do not know. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Read the whole sentence, then try your meaning in it. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If not, look at the clues again or check a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A jimmy is a short metal bar with a flat end, used to force open doors or windows.
fact: In the UK, the same tool is often called a «jemmy».
fact: To jimmy a door or window means to force it open with a bar or tool.
fact: Jimmy is also a short, friendly form of the name James, and a friendly or cheeky way to call a man you do not know in Scotland.
fact: In America, «jimmies» are tiny coloured sugar sprinkles on ice cream.
exercise: «The burglar used a jimmy to force open the back door.» What is a jimmy in this sentence? | A key that fits any lock | A small pet dog | *A short metal bar with a flat end | A kind of ice cream topping
exercise: «Mum jimmied the stuck lid off the paint tin.» What does jimmied mean here? | Painted over in a rush | Closed very quietly | *Forced open with a tool | Dropped on the floor
exercise: In Scotland, someone calls out, «Hey, Jimmy!» to a man they do not know. What does this suggest? | The man is a burglar | A police officer's name | A rude word that means go away | *A friendly or cheeky way to call a man
test: Jimmy is a short, friendly form of which name? | Jemmy | *James | Jim's cousin | John
test: «In America, ice cream comes with jimmies.» What are jimmies? | Cold drinks | *Tiny coloured sugar sprinkles | Metal bars used to open windows | Pairs of trousers
exam: In the sentence «The thief jimmied the window», what does jimmied mean? | *Forced open with a bar or tool | Painted | Looked through | Cleaned
